commit a9a348abe789991227d33c9aafb748fc3ecce65a
Author: Ali <ali@MacBook-Air-Ali.local>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 01:58:53 2026 +0500

    v6.54.0: hand off only after a finished turn; fix MCP/project-savings/alert edge cases
    
    - Auto handoff waits until Claude actually ends its turn (turnEnded), not
      during long tool calls, thinking or an unanswered question.
    - Terminal handoff uses a per-launch UUID file in new-sessions, deleted after
      start, so back-to-back handoffs don't overwrite each other; reports a
      missing claude binary instead of closing silently.
    - MCP savings_report no longer records "applied" on another project when the
      requested one isn't found; session_details returns an error for an unknown
      id or project instead of another session.
    - Project savings: "Hand to Claude" only copies the task; the fix date is set
      by "Mark as applied" or by Claude via MCP (step 4 of the prompt).
    - Don't announce the 5-hour reset when the weekly limit is also exhausted.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

