commit 9a86b787f180baaca971bc8e32a0b67386320269
Author: Ali <ali@MacBook-Air-Ali.local>
Date:   Thu Oct 29 22:35:15 2026 +0500

    v6.46.0: measured cache waste, weekly cache metric, exact limit and API error alerts
    
    - The Savings page's cache cause counts real cold-cache calls: the break
      outlasted that call's cache TTL and the next call rewrote the old context
      instead of reading it. Compacts are skipped, only the old context counts,
      priced as write minus read (1-hour cache costs more), limited to the period.
    - Weekly metric: a "Cache rewritten after going cold · 7 days" card with this
      week vs the previous 7 days. Daily totals go into project-savings.json
      (cacheDays), backfilled from the sessions in memory.
    - At 100% of a Claude limit: a "limit reached, resets at ..." notification and
      a pre-scheduled "limit reset" one at the reset time.
    - StopFailure hook: when a reply ends on an API error, a notification names
      the session and the cause (rate limit with reset time from account limits,
      overloaded, sign-in, billing, output too long). The notify hook now covers
      Notification and StopFailure; existing installs are upgraded on launch.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

