commit 62d879b6afe8065373a0325bb6a10a1fcda87488
Author: Ali <ali@MacBook-Air-Ali.local>
Date:   Thu Oct 29 21:56:49 2026 +0500

    v6.44.0: Claude writes its own handoff note before the context limit
    
    - When a session's context is within 15% (at least 20K) of the auto-handoff
      threshold, the app lists it in handoff-note-wanted.json; the
      UserPromptSubmit hook then asks Claude to end its reply with a hidden
      <!-- tk-handoff --> note (task, done, remaining, pending decision,
      important), in the conversation's language.
    - The handoff summary leads with that note and takes the session title
      from its "Task:" line; only the last prompt's reply counts. Without a
      note the mechanical summary is used as before.
    - The hook script exits without starting the app unless a redirect or a
      note request file exists. Turning off redirect now only clears pending
      redirects; turning off auto handoff removes the hook.
    - CHANGELOG also covers the two unversioned handoff commits before this.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

